Short. A first clause that runs long enough, past forty bytes, then cuts at this comma, and keeps going. Abbreviations like e.g. this one, i.e. that one, and etc. do not end sentences. Does a question end one? Yes! An ellipsis does too… And a closing paren (like this.) ends one as well.
A newline ends a clause too
even without punctuation. Here is a clause with no punctuation at all that keeps going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going and going until the cap cuts it on a space somewhere along the way
